WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.500
Lab 2 runs on your own test domain.

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.475
It hasn't been run by the authors.

3
00:00:04.475 --> 00:00:09.542
You need a test domain with at least one
test SQL Server instance, never production;

4
00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.825
a repository checkout, so the
Start Kit is beside the kit;

5
00:00:12.825 --> 00:00:17.178
PowerShell 7 with the Active Directory
module on a domain-joined machine;

6
00:00:17.178 --> 00:00:21.032
a network path to the instance's
port and U D P fourteen thirty-four;

7
00:00:21.032 --> 00:00:24.600
and a Windows login holding the
Start Kit's read permissions.

8
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.850
Never sysadmin.

9
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.616
Run the Start Kit's discovery,

10
00:00:27.616 --> 00:00:31.000
turn its output into the kit's
inventory, and classify it.

11
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.952
Compare each row with the
Start Kit's own first pass,

12
00:00:33.952 --> 00:00:38.100
add the owners' constraints and
application status, and classify again.

13
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.125
The second run is the one to keep.

14
00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:43.063
Nothing on the instance or
in the directory changes.

15
00:00:43.063 --> 00:00:46.458
To back it out, delete the lab's
files, and have the administrator

16
00:00:46.458 --> 00:00:49.730
remove the read permissions if
they were granted for the lab.
